# Docker build context for the JLineup Lambda images.
#
# This file is ALSO the input to the CDK asset fingerprint: DockerImageCode.fromImageAsset()
# hashes every file in the build context that is not ignored here. Anything that changes
# between builds (Gradle reports, test results, tmp dirs, IDE output, .DS_Store) would
# otherwise produce a new asset hash on every CI run, causing a fresh multi-GB image to be
# pushed into the CDK bootstrap ECR repository even when nothing relevant changed.
#
# Therefore: deny everything, then re-include exactly what the Dockerfiles COPY.
# Keep this in sync with the COPY instructions in Dockerfile, Dockerfile.chrome,
# Dockerfile.firefox and Dockerfile.webkit.

*

# Dockerfiles themselves must stay in the context
!Dockerfile
!Dockerfile.chrome
!Dockerfile.firefox
!Dockerfile.webkit

# Compiled handler classes    -> COPY build/classes/java/main ${LAMBDA_TASK_ROOT}
!build/classes/java/main

# Resources incl. logback.xml -> COPY build/resources/main ${LAMBDA_TASK_ROOT}
!build/resources/main

# Runtime dependencies        -> COPY build/output/lib/* ${LAMBDA_TASK_ROOT}/lib/
# (produced by the 'copyDependenciesToLib' task in lambda/build.gradle)
!build/output/lib
